[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.280]   This is an audio version of a Dave Kellogg post from April 30, 2008 titled Another Burned Unveiler,
[00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:10.880]   the UK's OGC. Branding always has its problems. Often, they're international in nature. Remember
[00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:16.000]   the UNIX systems vendor Arete? They had big problems in France where Arete means "stop."
[00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:20.320]   Who wants to buy the stock computer? Sometimes, they're cultural. I remember at Business Objects
[00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:24.640]   when the English product manager for BusinessMiner proposed a product icon that had two huge letters,
