[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.600]   This is an audio version of a Dave Kellogg post from April 8, 2009 titled "Welcome Uptick
[00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:09.840]   in Venture Capitalist Confidence." Thanks to this story in today's Mercury News,
[00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:13.840]   I noticed that Silicon Valley Venture Capitalist Confidence Index showed a welcome and rather
[00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:19.200]   surprising uptick in 1Q09. The index, produced by the University of San Francisco Entrepreneurship
[00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:25.120]   Program, has tracked venture capitalist confidence since 1Q04 and hit its all-time low 2.77 out of
[00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:32.000]   5 in 4Q08 and then rebounded somewhat in 1Q09 to 320.09. Exerpt, this quarter's reading
[00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:38.080]   rose from the previous quarter's reading of 2.77, a 5-year low, and ended a 5-quarter trend of new
[00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:43.120]   lows in confidence. This breaking of the downward trend in VC confidence provides hope for an
[00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:48.080]   eventual recovery in the high-growth venture environment. In fact, several of the VCs surveyed
[00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:52.240]   made the increasingly popular argument that the best companies are founded in bleak times,
[00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:57.040]   presumably as would-be entrepreneurs either flee or are laid off from their ailing employers.
[00:00:57.040 --> 00:01:01.360]   And some responding VCs see the downturn in the economy as an opportunity to build great
[00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:05.920]   companies. Prashant Shah of Hummerwind Blad Venture Partners shared, "In a struggling
[00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:10.160]   economy, the real innovators emerge. And for firms like ours who have capital,
[00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:14.880]   there is no better time to invest in new startups." And Sandy Miller of Institutional Venture
[00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:19.440]   Partners reasoned, "While the environment seems gloomy with no end in sight, we need to remember
[00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:24.160]   that some of the best companies have been founded and built during bleak times. True entrepreneurs
[00:01:24.160 --> 00:01:28.320]   will continue to find ways of moving their ideas forward." From a venture investor standpoint,
[00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:32.880]   2009 and 2010 should be an attractive environment for new investments, though there will be little
[00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:37.440]   liquidity for existing investments. For those wanting more detail, here's the full 1Q09
[00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:42.800]   Venture Capitalist Confidence Report (PDF). This audio version was created by Grant Duncan and AI
[00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:44.000]   with permission from Dave.
