[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.080]   This is an audio version of a Dave Kellogg post from April 27, 2011 titled "If we can
[00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:08.540]   have repeatable success, can we at least have repeatable failure?"
[00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:12.880]   I've always found business to have a fair amount of accidental, built-in hubris largely
[00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:15.400]   resulting from the strategy formulation process.
[00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:19.480]   I remember one time at Business Objects we had a strategy offsite where, in our infinite
[00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:23.600]   wisdom and with a fair bit of groupthink, we came up with the idea for a BI workflow
[00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:27.920]   solution which we dubbed Sundance for the name of the lovely venue at which it was conceived.
[00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:31.680]   I remember coming home from the offsite and having a conversation akin to the following,
[00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:33.080]   "Exec, what do you mean?
[00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:34.080]   Doesn't work.
[00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:35.080]   Me?
[00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:37.000]   Well, for example, what if nobody wants to buy it?"
[00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:39.800]   "Exec, what do you mean, what if nobody wants to buy it?"
[00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:40.880]   "It's strategic.
[00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:44.240]   We can put incentives in the Salesforce compensation plans and bundle it."
[00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:45.680]   "Don't worry, we can sell it."
[00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:49.160]   "Me, I didn't say what if no one wants to sell it, I said, what if no one wants to
[00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:50.160]   buy it?"
[00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:51.900]   "Exec, but it's strategic.
[00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:53.160]   We decided it at the offsite."
[00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:54.560]   "You're talking crazy, Dave.
[00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:55.560]   Come have another beer."
[00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:59.000]   As a marketer by background, I tend to view most everything as an experiment.
[00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:00.280]   That is the nature of marketing.
[00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:01.520]   You never know what's going to work.
[00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:04.720]   You can try different things, you can measure them, you can see what works and what does
