[00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:17.760]   The correlation is stunning.
[00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:22.160]   Taking some points off the line, 10% growth gets you an on-premises, like valuation of
[00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:28.000]   2x forward revenues, 20% growth gets you 3x 30% growth, gets you 3x 30% growth, gets
[00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:33.400]   you 4x 50% growth, gets you nearly 6x, basically in growth, rate front slash.
[00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:37.040]   You might think that profitability played some role in the valuation equation, but if
[00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:38.400]   you did, you're wrong.
[00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:44.080]   Let's demonstrate this by looking at CY13/EBITDA margins as reported by the same banker.
[00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:51.080]   Marketo MKTO 44% with A4 times revenue multiple Maron Software/MRION 40% with A4 times revenue
[00:00:51.080 --> 00:00:59.800]   multiple Workday/WD/AWDA 22% with AE1 11x revenue Multiple Bizarre Voice/BV 6% with
[00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:06.480]   AE5 times revenue Multiple Cornerstone on demand CADD 0% with A8 times revenue multiple
[00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:14.520]   CULIC Technologies QLI 0% with AE3 times revenue multiple Tango 017% with A3 times revenue
[00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:17.120]   multiple As you can see, there's basically no reward
[00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:18.420]   for profitability.
[00:01:18.420 --> 00:01:23.480]   In real estate, what matters is location, location, location, location, location, location,
