[00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:43.040]   contracts and renewing ones sign 1.5-year contracts, it would seem to indicate that
[00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:46.720]   renewing customers are indeed less bullish on future usage than X.
[00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:51.520]   Isting ones. Having drawn that conclusion, you are instantly tempted to blame the product,
[00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:56.080]   the customer success team, technical support, or some other factor for the customer's confidence
[00:00:56.080 --> 00:01:01.120]   reduction. But is there a confidence reduction? What does it actually mean when your renewals,
