[00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:03.920]   annual recurring revenue. In year 1, only the one-year deals come up for renewal, and since we've
[00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:08.800]   assumed everyone renews for the same length as their initial term, we have an ACD of one year.
[00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:14.400]   The VP of Sales is probably panicking. OMG, customers have cut their ACD from 2.3 to 1.0
[00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:19.120]   years. Who's to blame? What's gone wrong? Nothing. Only the one-year contracts had a shot
