[00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:29.600]   the initially renewing two-year contracts come up for renewal. The ACD is 1.7, again lower than the
[00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:35.120]   2.3-year new business, ACD. While, again, the decrease in ACD might lead you to suspect a
[00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:39.360]   problem, there is nothing wrong. It's just math and the fact that the shorter duration contracts
[00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:45.040]   renew more often which pulls down the renewals ACD. What to do about this? First, understand it.
[00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:50.320]   As with many SaaS metrics, it's counterintuitive. As I've mentioned before, SaaS metrics and unit
[00:02:50.320 --> 00:02:55.040]   economics are often misunderstood. While I remain a huge fan of using them to run the business,
[00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:58.640]   I strongly recommend taking the time to develop a deep understanding of them.
[00:02:58.640 --> 00:03:02.720]   In addition, the more I see counterintuitive examples, the more I believe in building full
