[00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:30.160]   rates for all nine combinations of 1Y, 2Y, 3Y, X1Y, 2Y, 3Y, 2Y, 3Y, 3Y deals for example,
[00:03:30.160 --> 00:03:36.080]   a 3Y to 1Y renewal rate. This will produce an overall renewal rate and an overall ACD for
[00:03:36.080 --> 00:03:40.880]   renewals. In a really good model, both the new business breakdown and the renewals matrix should
[00:03:40.880 --> 00:03:45.920]   vary by year. Armed with that model, built with assumptions based on both history and future goals
[00:03:45.920 --> 00:03:50.480]   for the new business breakdown and the renewals matrix, you can then have meaningful conversations
[00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:55.920]   how ACD is varying on new and renewals business relative to plan. Without that, by just looking
