[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.840]   This is an audio version of a Dave Kellogg post from April 28, 2015 titled, "Survivor
[00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:08.880]   bias in churn calculations, say it's not so."
[00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:12.280]   I was chatting with a fellow SaaS executive the other day and the conversation turned
[00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:13.960]   to churn and renewal rates.
[00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:18.120]   I asked how he calculated them and he said, "Well, we take every customer who is also
[00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:23.400]   a customer 12 months ago and then add up their ARR 12 months ago and add up their ARR today
[00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:27.760]   and then divide today's ARR by year ago ARR to get an overall retention or expansion
