[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.680]   This is an audio version of a Dave Kellogg post from July 20, 2016 titled, "We're
[00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:09.720]   not buddies, thoughts on managers too preoccupied with being liked."
[00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:13.400]   I always cringe when I hear a young parent say something like, "Hey buddy, don't forget
[00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:14.520]   your toy shovel."
[00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:18.800]   I feel the same way when I hear managers call subordinates "buddy," or when I see managers
