[00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:03.600]   that were supposed to come with them. Which phrase of the following sentence matters more?
[00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:08.160]   The first part or the second? We did what we were supposed to, but it didn't have the desired
[00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:13.280]   effect. We would have gotten the 30 MQLs from the event if it hadn't snowed in Boston. But who
[00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:17.680]   decided to tempt fate by doing a live event in Boston in February? People who want to be judged
[00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:22.800]   on intentions think about the snowstorm. People who want to be judged on results think about the MQLs.
[00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:26.880]   People who want to be judged on intentions build in what they see as reasons, which others
[00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:32.080]   typically see as excuses, which others typically see as excuses for results not being achieved.
[00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:36.400]   I'm six months late hiring the PR manager, but that's because it's hard to find great PR people
