[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.520]   This is an audio version of a Dave Kellogg post from December 15th, 2018 titled "7 Books
[00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:10.560]   Not to Give the Boss for Christmas Ass." Note, this post includes images. See the original post
[00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:15.440]   on Kellblog for visuals. Well, when you run a company focused on corporate finance, you don't
[00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:21.360]   get a lot of holiday party scandals. At hosts, very nice 2018 holiday party. The closest thing
[00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:26.400]   we had was an employee conversing with me about books, Bad Blood, and then wholeheartedly suggesting
[00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:31.360]   that I just had to read another book, Drive, which, as it turns out, is about motivating
[00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:35.920]   employees. Hum. The blowback potential hadn't occurred to me in real time, but after I got
[00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:39.840]   home I noticed an email from the person who'd suggested the book, contritely offering that the
[00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:44.720]   suggestion wasn't intended to send a message or anything. I laughed. My reply was simple. I once
[00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:48.160]   actually not just recommended, but actually bought and gave death by meeting to my boss,
