[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.480]   This is an audio version of a Dave Kellogg post from January 30, 2019 titled Rule of
[00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:07.580]   40 Glideslope Planning.
[00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:09.780]   Enterprise SaaS companies need a lot of money to grow.
[00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:15.720]   The median company spends $1.32 to acquire $1.10 in annual recurring revenue (ARR).
[00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:19.160]   They need to make that investment for 14 years before getting to an IPO.
[00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:23.580]   It all adds up to a median of $300 million in capital raised prior to an IPO.
[00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:28.260]   With such vast amounts of money in play, some say it's a growth at all costs game.
